## 7. Architecture Boundaries

Before scaffolding code, define the initial feature/layer map in [Architecture Layering v0.1](./architecture-layering-v0.1.md).

Rules that should hold from the first implementation:

- lower layers must not import runtime, UI, transport, persistence, provider SDK, or framework boundary concerns unless that layer owns the boundary.
- cross-cutting concerns should enter through explicit providers or interfaces.
- hand-written product source files use 700 lines as the default maintainability threshold; extract a cohesive layer, route, component, or helper before exceeding it.{% if backend_stack == 'rust' %}
- exception: Rust modules are organized by domain and are exempt from the generic line limit.{% endif %}{% if swift_app_stack | default('none') == 'ios' %}
- SwiftUI views render state and emit actions; persistence, file I/O, networking, and multi-step workflows belong behind injected protocols and adapters.
- `{{ swift_project_spec_path }}` owns Xcode project structure, and one explicitly created fixed simulator owns routine local XCTest evidence.{% endif %}

## 8. Validation Strategy

Use `./scripts/validate-changed-scope.mjs` before marking local implementation work complete. Use `./scripts/finalize.sh` as the check-only CI/pre-merge full gate.

Run `./scripts/smoke.sh` after changes to startup, routing, environment wiring, or cross-service integration.{% if frontend_stack != 'none' %}

Explicitly evaluate Playwright E2E for this frontend. Enable it after the frontend can start reliably and at least one stable user journey exists; otherwise record the deferral reason. See [E2E Testing Task](../tasks/e2e-testing.md).
{% endif %}{% if swift_app_stack | default('none') == 'ios' %}

Use `./scripts/test.mjs` for XCTest so local and CI destination policy stays centralized. Treat simulator UI tests as deterministic evidence only when fixtures are isolated from developer data. See [iOS Testing Task](../tasks/ios-testing.md).{% endif %}

